hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1226","Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Hussein narrated to us, on the authority of his father, Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, he said: I heard Abu Buraidah, He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “In man there are three hundred and sixty joints, so he must give alms for each joint.” Charity.” He said: Who can bear that, O Prophet of God? He said: “You bury someone who murmurs in the mosque, or you move something out of the way, but if you are not able to perform it, then two rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer will suffice.”"
